---
// /research — the research corpus map, rendered from the frozen corpus source. Promoted to a
// top-level nav slot in the 2026-08-03 reorg; supersedes the v0.1 that lived at
// /how-these-documents-relate (which now 301s here).
//
// WHAT THIS PAGE IS, AND WHAT WENT WRONG WITH SAYING SO (Repair Unit 3, 2026-08-23).
//
// The body is a SNAPSHOT. It was written on 2026-08-03 and has not changed since, and its sentences
// are in the present tense: "Everything below is published, versioned, and DOI'd", "The Theory of
// Data — Version 4.0 …, the canonical manuscript". Every one of those was true the day it was
// written. Several are not true now — ToD is at v6.1, the Introduction at v2.2, Frame-QL's
// Introduction at v2.3 — and the map is byte-frozen, so they will go on saying what they say.
//
// THE DEFECT WAS NOT THE BODY. Ruling 8 (2026-08-21) already demoted this file from publication
// authority and ruled explicitly against rewriting it; reconciliation row
// `rc-research-corpus-map-not-authority` records that its statements are "accurate as of its own
// edition date and not maintained against the record". That contract existed and was correct — and
// it was INVISIBLE. A reader arrived at a page whose only date was `v0.3 · August 2026`, which reads
// as a version stamp on the map rather than as a bound on everything the map claims, and could
// reasonably read four-week-old currency claims as present-tense ones. This is the smallest framing
// that makes the page's contract truthful to that reader; not one byte of the snapshot moves.
//
// REGISTER (house rule v0.3 §4.3, and Huayin's Unit 3 classification).
//   · The orientation line below the kicker is TEACHING. Plain register, one sentence, no typed
//     vocabulary: it exists so the misreading cannot happen, and it happens BEFORE the body because
//     that is where the misreading would.
//   · "This snapshot" at the foot is the EDITION/STATUS FACT, and it is the page's only typed block —
//     visibly bounded by its rule, in the same position and the same class the deposited-edition
//     routes use for "This edition". It states what is rendered, when, that the body is preserved
//     rather than maintained, and where current records live.
//
// THE EDITION THIS PAGE CAN TRUTHFULLY NAME IS v0.3, NOT v0.2. The filename says `v0_2` and the
// registry, the ledger and Ruling 8 all refer to it by that path — but the filename is stale, frozen
// at creation. The body has declared **v0.3** since f27318d, which bumped it deliberately (0.2 → 0.3)
// in the same commit that wrote the Version 4.0 sentence, and `v0.3 · August 2026` is what the page
// has been showing readers ever since. Chrome that said "v0.2" would contradict the line printed six
// lines below it. The filename is not renamed here: it is the registry's key for a frozen consumer.
//
// THE DATE IS REPO PROVENANCE, STATED NARROWLY. The snapshot declares "August 2026" and no day. The
// repository establishes the day — 09891a4, 2026-08-03, the last commit to touch the file, with no
// commit since — so the chrome says the month the snapshot declares and adds the preservation date as
// what it is: a fact about this repository, not a claim the snapshot makes about itself.
//
// NO PUBLICATION FACTS ARE AUTHORED HERE. The current-records pointer is a LINK to /about, which
// renders CHRONOLOGICAL_SELECTION from the registry. No DOI, version or date of any deposit is typed
// into this file, so this route states no publication fact and needs no consumer permission — the
// ownership boundary settled in Unit 2.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content } from '../content/corpus/research_corpus_map_v0_2.md';

// Declared by the snapshot itself (line 5 of the source); the day comes from repo history.
const SNAPSHOT_EDITION = 'v0.3';
const SNAPSHOT_DECLARED_DATE = 'August 2026';
const SNAPSHOT_PRESERVED_SINCE = '3 August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="The research corpus — datumwise"
  description="How the datumwise documents relate — the research corpus, mapped, as it was written in August 2026: the theory, the proved kernel, the introductions, the positions, the ripples, and the engine. A preserved snapshot; current publication records are on the About page.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Research</p>
    <p class="orientation">
      This page keeps an earlier map of the research corpus exactly as it was written. It is a
      snapshot rather than a running index — several of the documents it describes have been
      published in newer editions since. For what is current, see the publication list on
      <a href="/about">About</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose research">
    <Content />
  </article>

  <p class="evidence-note">
    <strong>This snapshot.</strong> This page renders the research map as it was at
    <strong>{SNAPSHOT_EDITION}</strong>, dated <strong>{SNAPSHOT_DECLARED_DATE}</strong> by the map
    itself and unchanged in this repository since {SNAPSHOT_PRESERVED_SINCE}. The text is preserved
    as written, not updated: the versions, dates and DOIs it names were accurate to that snapshot and
    are not maintained as pointers to whatever is current, so some of them now name superseded
    editions. The current record for every document is kept in the publication registry and rendered
    on <a href="/about">About</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 0 auto; }
  .kicker { color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .orientation { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .evidence-note { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 3rem auto 0; padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
